{"ts": "2026-11-23T10:42:34.543522Z", "run_id": "r-20261123T0928Z-3bb6", "unit": "openspec:add-mcp-client", "seq": 63, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-006", "id": "Q-006", "status": "answered", "reason": "Verified in the files: policy_decision has FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY with a tenant policy and only the app role is granted SELECT; roles.ts creates both roles NOBYPASSRLS; discover.db.test.ts lines 261-277 read through ownerPool with no set_config; withTenantTx sets app.tenant_id per transaction and is exported from src/tenancy/index.ts; sibling tests (src/pdp/log-own-tx.db.test.ts) read the same table through withTenantTx(db.appPool, ctx, ...). The clarifier suggestion is the repository's established pattern and the only change needed, and it is the sole route that unfreezes the test file.", "called": true, "tasks": ["4.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.4551719999999997, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "a49e257d9abad90dc186bf6f63404fdc9aca239c9e8f878beb74a7eb6ffbedb0", "checked": [{"ref": "src/db/migrations/0110_policy_decision.sql:21", "quote": "ALTER TABLE ursitoare.policy_decision FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;", "claim": "Row level security is forced on policy_decision, so even the table owner is filtered by the tenant policy."}, {"ref": "src/db/migrations/0110_policy_decision.sql:23", "quote": "USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id', true))", "claim": "A session that sets no app.tenant_id sees no rows of policy_decision."}, {"ref": "src/db/roles.ts:12", "quote": "const ROLE_ATTRIBUTES = \"LOGIN NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE NOREPLICATION NOBYPASSRLS\";", "claim": "The owner role cannot bypass row level security, so ownerPool reads are filtered."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/discover.db.test.ts:263", "quote": "const r = await d.ownerPool.query<{ n: number }>(", "claim": "rowCount queries the owner pool directly without a tenant setting, so it always counts zero."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/discover.db.test.ts:271", "quote": "const r = await d.ownerPool.query<{ decision: string; errors: string[]; permit: unknown }>(", "claim": "newRows also reads through the owner pool without a tenant setting and is always empty."}, {"ref": "src/tenancy/tx.ts:21", "quote": "await client.query(\"SELECT set_config('app.tenant_id', $1, true)\", [ctx.tenantId]);", "claim": "withTenantTx sets app.tenant_id inside the transaction, which makes the policy let the tenant's rows through."}, {"ref": "src/tenancy/index.ts:8", "quote": "export { withTenantTx } from \"./tx.ts\";", "claim": "withTenantTx is importable from the tenancy index as the suggestion requires."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/log-own-tx.db.test.ts:141", "quote": "return withTenantTx(db.appPool, ctx, async (tx) => {", "claim": "The existing test of recordDecisionOwnTx reads policy_decision through withTenantTx on the app pool, the same pattern as option 1."}, {"ref": "src/pdp/log.ts:151", "quote": "return withTenantTx(pool, ctx, (tx) => recordDecision(tx, ctx, decision, req, extra));", "claim": "recordDecisionOwnTx writes the decision in a tenant transaction, so the rows exist and are readable under the tenant context."}]}
